<title>UK: Honduras seeks to improve coffee processsing.</title>
<headline>Honduras seeks to improve coffee processsing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Honduras minister on Wednesday held talks with U.N. Common Fund for Commodities officials in Amsterdam where he stressed the need for Honduras to improve the processing of coffee and develop gourmet coffee.</p>
<p>Foreign Minister Delmer Urbizo Panting, on an European tour, was also quoted by a Common Fund statement as saying that the Latin American state also planned to diversify the commodity base through growing fruit.</p>
<p>Panting also spoke of the need &quot;to correct market failures in several commodity markets in Central America,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The Amsterdam-based Common Fund finances commodity development projects in developing nations. --Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
